{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they shall be ashamed. Flutes.</b> Some say from the root משרק [Berakhot 18], but the correct view is that it is the eye of shoresh 'flute,' and likewise השרוקים (Zechariah 1:8)." "<b>White ones.</b> The bricks, and it is a noun of attribute, or the yod is a plural marker, and it ought to have been חורים, and like it is חורי יהודה (Jeremiah 27:20):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The lemma 'ובשו' (they shall be ashamed) does not fit the comment about flutes; this appears to be a textual difficulty, possibly a displaced lemma. Translated hyper-literally without smoothing. The bracketed Berakhot 18 citation is uncertain as the reference does not correspond to a known discussion of משרק in Berakhot."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:18.202385156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}